{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:b925a02df1aa4bb6","name":"Emergency Crew","source":{"id":"source:reference-b925a02df1aa4bb6","title":"Emergency Crew","revision":23073,"timestamp":"2024-09-15T13:33:16Z","sha256":"af2fb78ac6a020c7f11aba1b7a686788f889552f7d45955fecaf395be0035566","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=23073","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Emergency%20Crew&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-b925a02df1aa4bb6","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Threats of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Threats_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["There's nothing easy about fighting in space. When the shields fail, when laser blasts rock the ship and fires rage out of control, it falls to the Emergency Crew to keep the ship together long enough for the real engineers and techs to come in and put the ship back together again. A ship's Emergency Crew also has the dubious honor of defending a vessel when it's boarded by enemy forces. So in addition to putting out fires and getting systems up and running, it is responsible for holding off pirates, Stormtroopers, and any other force that intends to take over the ship. Part firefighter, part technician, and part warrior, the Emergency Crews are the first line of defense when a ship becomes imperiled.\n"]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Emergency Crew Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["The Emergency Crew is the first response to any danger a ship faces. These are the individuals who work to extract an injured ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"}," pilot from his damaged ship, who put out the flames when the ship is struck by a torpedo, and who give their lives to defend the rest of the crew when intruders blast their way inside to take the ship by force.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["An Emergency Crew team consists of four to six members. The various crews might be broken into different functions, such as fire brigade, security, and mechanics. Leading each team is a specialist-soldier, technician, or engineer- who can put these crew members to best use. Despite the fact that these teams might have different primary functions, each is expected to pitch in whenever the ship is in danger.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Emergency Crew Statistics (CL 1)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 4\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +2; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +2\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Binary"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Binary","referenceId":"reference:ee1c8277caf5fb9b"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 14 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 14), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 10, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Will Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Will_Defense"},": 10\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},": 9, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Threshold"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Threshold"},": 10\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children